{
  "name": "DecimalIsANumber",
  "comment": "A type's kind is a type (ruling 1). A number carrying kind=decimal lands a value whose\ntype is number and whose kind navigates as the \"decimal\" type: `%n!type.kind.name%` is\n\"decimal\". Written in formal so the builder's Type choice is out of it — the red is the\nruntime's: today `%n!type.kind%` reads as a text \"decimal\" (the stopgap of decision 707),\nso `.name` can't be navigated.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "variable.set(Name=%n%, Value=\"1.5\", Type={name:\"number\", kind:\"decimal\"})",
      "line": {
